3. distinguish at least attested, inferred, interpretive, speculative, and counterfactual material;
4. keep semantic deltas directional;
5. expose known loss for cross-language or cross-domain exchange;
6. permit multiple deposits for one surface token;
7. avoid silently deleting superseded or challenged states;
8. make packet compression traceable back to source deposits;
9. separate semantic confidence from external factual verification;
10. provide a method to export the active Meaning Receipt used for a consequential action.

An implementation claiming MBIP-Reality v0.1 SHOULD additionally support all RK-12 fields and CoSequence links.

